WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.100
-It is time to play a game of deception called

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.801
"True Confessions."

00:00:04.801 --> 00:00:06.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:13.601
♪♪

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:16.434
My first opponent tonight is an award-winning actress

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:18.067
who stars in the new Netflix series

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.200
"Inventing Anna."

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:21.367
Please welcome Laverne Cox!

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:24.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:27.501
You floated in. You floated --

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:30.567
Welcome. You kind of floated in.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.734
Laverne and I will be facing off

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:35.200
against a multi-talented actor and director.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.834
His new series, "Severance,"

00:00:36.834 --> 00:00:39.834
can be seen every Friday on Apple TV Plus.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:42.634
Please welcome Ben Stiller!

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:45.434
Wow! That's --Whoa!

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:48.033
Equally -- Equally, beautifully.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.267
What an entrance. Equally beautiful.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.534
Good to see you, pal. -Nice to see you.

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:54.100
-Guys, this is how each of this works.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.200
In front of each of us

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.167
are two envelopes containing confessions.

00:00:57.167 --> 00:00:59.400
One is true. The other is a lie.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.067
Once you read your confession, the other two players

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.434
get to interrogate you,

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:04.200
then they have to come up to a unanimous decision.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.434
Is it a truth? Or is it a lie?

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:08.734
Laverne, you're going to go first.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.667
Which envelope should she open?

00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:12.067
-I'm holding up... -What do you think, Ben?

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.567
-...two envelopes.

00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:14.868
-Two. -Right. Okay.

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:16.234
-Two. Right? -Good.

00:01:16.234 --> 00:01:17.934
-We didn't do this. -So that wasn't prearranged.

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.367
-No, that wasn't --

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:21.801
-See? Is this how it is at the restaurant when you're ordering?

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:23.567
-Oh, my God.

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:24.901
-[ Clears throat ]

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:27.300
-When I got "Orange is the New Black,"

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.133
I celebrated with a nice dinner.

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:33.601
But then my card was declined, which is ironic

00:01:33.601 --> 00:01:38.300
because my character was in jail for credit-card fraud.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:42.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:44.634
-Alright. -That's irony, right?

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:47.100
-Now, what year was this?

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.734
"Orange is the New Black" was what?

00:01:48.734 --> 00:01:51.000
-So, we shot the first season in 2012,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.934
so that was 10 years ago.

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:57.634
And the first season premiered in 2013.

00:01:57.634 --> 00:02:00.901
But when I booked the show in 2012,

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:02.167
it was an intense year for me,

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.767
and I've actually talked about this before publicly.

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.167
It was the year I turned 40.

00:02:05.167 --> 00:02:07.000
I was actually gonna stop acting

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.968
because I was in rent arrears in February of 2012.

00:02:09.968 --> 00:02:11.334
-I feel like you're talking a lot.

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:14.767
-She's talking too much. Yeah. There's too much detail.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.334
I asked one question, right?

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.601
-Do you want to ask me a question?

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:20.934
-Yeah. -Ask me a question.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:23.868
-Why were you declined? Why was it declined?

00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:26.300
-Why is anybody's credit card declined?

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:27.634
-That's true. I don't know --

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:28.667
I don't know exactly why -- -Didn't have any money.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:29.834
-Didn't have any money.

00:02:29.834 --> 00:02:32.968
-What year were credit cards invented?

00:02:32.968 --> 00:02:35.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.033
-See? He throws you off.

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:38.767
He throws you off with those questions.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.000
-So, Mr. Stiller, I know I'm a woman

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.868
of a certain age, but I'm not that old.

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:45.534
-No, yeah. -Okay. I have a question.

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.901
Simple question. What was the restaurant?

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.133
-The restaurant is this restaurant called L'Express

00:02:50.133 --> 00:02:51.467
here in New York City.

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:56.234
I ordered the grilled salmon that you put on a salad,

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:59.801
but without the salad because it was lighter and cheaper

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:02.367
than the salmon that you would get as an entrée,

00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:05.334
and then that would have a lot of shredded Parmesan cheese

00:03:05.334 --> 00:03:08.834
on the salmon -- -Doesn't sound like something

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:11.334
that no one with a credit card would order normally.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:12.968
Just saying.

00:03:12.968 --> 00:03:15.634
-Like the pièce de résistance, she orders their French fries,

00:03:15.634 --> 00:03:17.734
'cause they're my favorite French fries in the city.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:19.167
They're so delicious. Do you know --

00:03:19.167 --> 00:03:20.634
You know the French fries at L'Express.

00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:22.000
-The frites.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.267
-They're really good French fries.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:24.667
-French fries, yes. -Pommes frite.

00:03:24.667 --> 00:03:28.400
-Pommes frite. I am saying absolutely that this is a lie.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.100
-Lie. Total lie.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.501
-Laverne Cox.

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:34.400
Is it the truth or is it a lie?

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.834
[ Drum roll ]

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:36.968
-It's a lie.

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:39.133
-Whoa! We did it! -Whoo!

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:42.300
♪♪

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.701
-Okay. It is my turn right now. Which envelope should I open?

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:47.534
One or two? -[ Audience shouting, "One" ]

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.167
-One. One.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:52.901
-I was one of the voices on U2's hit song "Vertigo."

00:03:52.901 --> 00:03:55.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:58.100
[ Cox laughing ]

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.801
-What year was the song released?

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:02.100
-The song?

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:07.467
It was released -- It's got to be 2005 or something.

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:09.133
-Right. That sounds like -- Right, yeah.

00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:11.167
-This was -- Yeah. -How did it happen?

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:15.968
-[ Chuckles ] I was at a party with Bono.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:18.100
-[ Laughter ] -That's believable.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.400
-Michael Stipe was one of the people there.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.234
We had a bunch of friends hanging out,

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:24.033
and he was talking about he was recording his new album.

00:04:24.033 --> 00:04:25.501
I said, "Cool."

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.234
And he goes, "Let me play you a song,"

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:30.501
and he played me "Vertigo" on his phone.

00:04:30.501 --> 00:04:33.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.634 --> 00:04:35.501
And so -- -I want to cross-check this

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:37.501
with the invention of the iPhone.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.100
-Yeah. I don't know --

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.667
I don't know if it was an iPhone.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:42.467
-There were no iPhones in 2004, obviously.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.133
-Are you gonna play it on a BlackBerry?

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:47.701
-I think it was an mp3 player. Maybe not a phone.

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:49.634
It was something. -And now -- Okay.

00:04:49.634 --> 00:04:52.000
I'm a little confused. Everything's changing now.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.167
-So he goes, "But I want to add some part here

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:56.100
after 'Hello, hello.'

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.367
And he goes, "I want to say 'hello!'

00:04:58.367 --> 00:05:01.501
Can we get all of you to scream "hello"?

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:04.234
We called his phone and left a message on his phone.

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:06.567
And I go, "Hola!"

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.534 --> 00:05:10.601
And what you hear on the record

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:14.567
is me on Bono's voicemail singing "Hola!"

00:05:14.567 --> 00:05:16.400
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.501 --> 00:05:22.200
-I -- -Hola!

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:23.868
-Right.

00:05:23.868 --> 00:05:26.033
-♪ Hello, hello! ♪

00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:27.534
Hola!

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:29.801
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.801 --> 00:05:31.834
-I think it's true.

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:33.467
-I think it's true, as well.

00:05:33.467 --> 00:05:34.701
[ Drum roll ]

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.901
-It is a lie. I was never in that song.

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:38.000
-Whoa.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:39.133
♪♪

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:41.934
Wow. -Not bad.

00:05:41.934 --> 00:05:45.534
Here we go right now. Ben, it is your -- Yeah.

00:05:45.534 --> 00:05:48.567
I will say for, Ben Stiller, number one or two?

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:49.901
Alright. So we're going number two?

00:05:49.901 --> 00:05:51.501
-Alright. Do number two. -He's a legend.

00:05:51.501 --> 00:05:52.834
-Thank you.

00:05:52.834 --> 00:05:56.634
[ Chuckles ] Um...

00:05:56.634 --> 00:05:58.701
-He laughs as he looks at it.

00:06:01.167 --> 00:06:04.934
-I almost made a movie with Mick Jagger.

00:06:04.934 --> 00:06:08.734
-What movie did you almost make with Mick Jagger?

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.367
-This is similar to my story.

00:06:10.367 --> 00:06:13.601
-Um, I almost made a movie with Mick Jagger

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:17.567
that was a concert film

00:06:17.567 --> 00:06:20.400
that I was going to direct

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.701
and act in with myself and Brad Pitt.

00:06:23.701 --> 00:06:25.868
Based on the story that these two super fans

00:06:25.868 --> 00:06:28.968
were following the Rolling Stones all around,

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:32.767
and I was one and Brad Pitt was the other one and --

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:33.968
-[ Laughter ] -And we were --

00:06:33.968 --> 00:06:35.868
-I've known you for a long time,

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:38.000
and I know that you love crazy stories.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.834
-Wow. -No, no, no. Yeah. Right.

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:41.868
-You have some crazy stories.

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.367
Didn't you -- You once almost fought

00:06:43.367 --> 00:06:44.734
Boom Boom Mancini in the ring.

00:06:44.734 --> 00:06:47.901
-[ Laughs ] I did. I alm-- I was going to a boxing gym.

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:50.334
-Boom Boom Mancini, were they on the --

00:06:50.334 --> 00:06:52.801
"Flintstones"? Boom Boom Mancini?

00:06:52.801 --> 00:06:54.434
-No. The boxer. -It's a boxing champion.

00:06:54.434 --> 00:06:55.934
-Famous boxer.

00:06:55.934 --> 00:06:57.334
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:58.467
You're thinking of Bamm-Bamm.

00:06:58.467 --> 00:07:00.868
-That sounds like a lie. Oh, Bamm-Bamm.

00:07:00.868 --> 00:07:02.834
-Yeah. Boom Boom. Bamm-Bamm. Wait. Sorry.

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:05.133
This has nothing to do with Boom Boom or Bamm-Bamm.

00:07:05.133 --> 00:07:06.968
-So, this definitely happened.

00:07:06.968 --> 00:07:10.033
We were going to do this film where we follow them around,

00:07:10.033 --> 00:07:13.234
and Mick actually -- It was his idea,

00:07:13.234 --> 00:07:14.868
and he wanted to do the film and --

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:16.200
-What did he say to you?

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.067
[as Jagger] "Let's go. I got to do a movie with you."

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:19.467
-Right. Yeah. But I've got convince --

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:21.100
I'll tell you what to say, you do the --

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:22.567
-[Normal voice] You tell me what to say. He says what?

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:25.667
-He said, "I think this is a great idea for a concert film."

00:07:25.667 --> 00:07:28.467
-"I really think it's a great idea for a concert film."

00:07:28.467 --> 00:07:31.434
-"But I've got to convince the rest of the band."

00:07:31.434 --> 00:07:35.000
-"But! I gotta convince the rest of the band!"

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.000
-"'Cause Keith really isn't into it."

00:07:37.000 --> 00:07:40.100
-♪ Keith isn't into it, Keith isn't into it ♪

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:43.534
♪ I can't convince him, man, 'cause Keith isn't into it ♪

00:07:43.534 --> 00:07:44.868
♪ Yeah! ♪

00:07:44.868 --> 00:07:46.100
[Normal voice] Now...

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.901
I don't know. I don't know about this.

00:07:47.901 --> 00:07:49.734
What do you think? What year was it?

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:52.300
-That's exactly how it happened. -Yeah.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:57.100
-This was, like, 1992, 1993.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:01.200
-This is so believable that I think it's not believable.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.567
-I think he's lying.

00:08:02.567 --> 00:08:04.467
-What do you guys think? -What do you think?

00:08:04.467 --> 00:08:05.968
[ Audience shouts, "Lie" ]

00:08:05.968 --> 00:08:08.434
-They think lie. Wait. But -- Alright.

00:08:08.434 --> 00:08:12.567
Ben Stiller, we're all gonna say it's a lie.

00:08:12.567 --> 00:08:14.234
[ Drum roll ]

00:08:14.234 --> 00:08:16.734
-It's a lie? -Is it?

00:08:16.734 --> 00:08:18.300
-It's true!

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.334
-[ Cheers and applause ] -He's the best!

00:08:20.334 --> 00:08:23.968
That's why he's the greatest! That's why he's the greatest!

00:08:23.968 --> 00:08:28.834
That is why Ben Stiller is the greatest, right there.

00:08:28.834 --> 00:08:32.400
-I told you he's a legend. -"True Confessions," everybody.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:35.234
My thanks to Laverne Cox and Ben Stiller.

00:08:35.234 --> 00:08:36.834
"True Confessions."

00:08:36.834 --> 00:08:38.567
We're talking to Ben more after the break.

00:08:38.567 --> 00:08:40.634
Stick around. All truth from now on.

